hadiths[70]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2283","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Bakr bin Ayyash: We entered upon Abu Hasin to visit him, and Asim was with us. He said: Abu Hasin said to Asim: ""Do you remember a hadith that Qasim bin Mukhaymira narrated to us?"" He said: ""Yes, he narrated to us one day from Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'When the Muslim servant falls ill, Allah, the Exalted, says to those who write: ""Write for him the best of what he used to do when he was healthy, until I free him.""'"
"2284","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): He said: ""When the believer falls ill, Allah purifies him just as the bellows purges the impurities from iron."
"2285","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Amr: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When a man comes to visit a sick person, let him say: 'O Allah, heal Your servant, so he may inflict harm upon an enemy for You, or walk for You to the prayer.'"" And in a narration: ""...to a funeral."
"2286","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik: That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""When any of you has a fever, let cold water be poured over him for three nights during the Sahar (pre-dawn)."
"2287","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir, who said: ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah and Sahl ibn Ḥunayf set out intending to bathe. They went looking for a secluded place. ʿĀmir (the text in the Musnad reads ""Sahl,"" and that is the correct reading) removed a woolen cloak he was wearing. I looked at him and struck him with the evil eye. He went down to the water to bathe. I heard a gurgling sound from him in the water. I came to him and called him three times, but he did not answer me. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He came walking, wading into the water—it is as if I am looking at the whiteness of his shins. He struck his chest with his hand and said: ""O Allah, remove from him its heat, its chill, and its suffering."" He stood up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When one of you sees from his brother, or from himself, or from his wealth something that amazes him, let him invoke blessing upon it (say: Bārak Allāh fīh), for the evil eye is real."""
"2288","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: If you hear of the plague in a land, do not enter it, and if it breaks out in a land where you are, do not leave it (fleeing from it). And in a narration: This illness or sickness is a punishment with which some nations before you were tormented, (or a group from the Children of Israel), then it remained afterward in the land, going away one time and coming another. So whoever hears of it in a land must not approach it, and whoever is in a land where it occurs, fleeing from it must not make him leave. This is narrated from the hadith of Usāmah bin Zayd, Saʿd bin Abī Waqqāṣ, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān bin ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"2289","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: If the blood becomes agitated in any of you, let him perform cupping, for indeed blood, when it boils over in a person, kills him."
"2290","[AI-translation] Narrated Umm Salamah: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) saw a slave-girl in her house with a discoloration on her face, so he said: Seek ruqyah for her, for indeed she has the look (the evil eye)."
"2291","[AI-translation] Narrated Muhammad bin Qays: Abu Hurayrah was asked, ""Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) regarding omens in three things: in the dwelling, the horse, and the woman?"" He said, ""In that case, I would be attributing to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) what he did not say. But I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: The truest omen is the good omen, and the evil eye is true."
"2292","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah visited a sick person and said, ""Have you not called a physician for him?"" They said, ""O Messenger of Allah, do you command us to do this?"" He said: ""Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down a disease except that He sent down along with it its cure."
"2293","[AI-translation] Narrated Zuhayr (meaning Ibn Mu'awiyah) from his wife: She heard Mulaykah bint 'Umar - and he mentioned that she returned the sheep to its owners during the emirate of 'Umar bin al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) - that she prepared for her, for an illness she had, cow's ghee, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Its milk is a healing, its ghee is a medicine, and its meat is a disease. Meaning the cow."
"2294","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Rimthah: I set out with my father towards the Prophet (peace be upon him)... He said: My father said to him: Show me this which is on your back, for I am a physician. He said: Allah is the Physician; rather, you are a compassionate man. Its Physician is the One who created it."
"2295","[AI-translation] Darda' (marfu'an): Allah created the disease and the cure, so seek treatment, but do not seek treatment with what is unlawful."
"2296","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): Allah, Mighty and Majestic, did not send down a disease except that He sent down for it a cure, except old age. So adhere to the milk of cows, for it grazes from every tree."
"2297","[AI-translation] Khudri (marfu'an): Allah did not send down a disease - or did not create a disease - except that He sent down - or created - for it a cure; whoever knows it, knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it, is ignorant of it, except as-sam. They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what is as-sam?"" He said: ""Death."
"2298","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Indeed, there is healing in the 'Ajwah of al-'Aliyah, or indeed it is an antidote first thing in the morning."
"2299","[AI-translation] Muqanna', then he said: ""I will not leave until you are cupped, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'Indeed, there is healing in it.'"
"2300","[AI-translation] Juhani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""If there is healing in anything, it is in the incision of a cupping horn, or a drink of honey, or a cauterization that touches the pain, and I dislike cauterization and do not love it."
"2301","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""If there is good in anything with which you seek treatment, it is cupping."
"2302","[AI-translation] Muqanna', then he said: ""I will not leave until you are cupped, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: 'If there is good in any of your medicines, it is in the incision of a cupping horn, or a drink of honey, or a burn of fire, and I do not love to be cauterized.'"
"2303","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: ""If there is any true evil omen, it is in the woman, the horse, and the house."
"2304","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, raised to the Prophet: ""Indeed, it is blessed; indeed, it is nourishing food."" He meant: Zamzam."
"2305","[AI-translation] 'Abd Allah ibn Buraydah said: I heard my father saying: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, spat on the leg of 'Amr ibn Mu'adh when his leg was cut off, and it healed."
"2306","[AI-translation] From Usamah ibn Sharik, who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""The black seed is a healing for every disease except death."
"2307","Ibn ʿUmar said: “O Nāfiʿ, blood has become agitated in me, so find me a cupper and make him gentle, if you can, and do not make him an old man or a young boy. For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Cupping on an empty stomach is best; in it there is healing and blessing, and it increases the intellect and memory. So get cupped with the blessing of Allah on Thursday, and avoid cupping on Wednesday, Friday, Saturday, and Sunday as a precaution. And get cupped on Monday and Tuesday, for that is the day on which Allah cured Ayyūb of the affliction, and He struck him with the affliction on Wednesday. Indeed, neither leprosy nor vitiligo appears except on Wednesday or the night of Wednesday.’”"
"2308","[AI-translation] From Samurah, raised to the Prophet: ""The best thing with which you seek treatment is cupping."
"2309","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas (marfu'): The best with which you treat yourselves is cupping and sea costus, and do not torment your children by pressing."
"2310","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn Abbas (marfu'): The best day on which you get cupped is the seventeenth, the nineteenth, and the twenty-first. And he said: I did not pass by any company of angels on the night I was taken on the Night Journey except they said: Upon you is cupping, O Muhammad!"
"2311","[AI-translation] Narrated from a man of the Ansar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, visited a man who had a wound, and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Call for him the physician of Banu So-and-so. He said: So he was called and he came, and he said: O Messenger of Allah! Does medicine avail anything? He said: Glory be to Allah! Has Allah sent down any disease in the earth except that He made a cure for it?"
"2312","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas bin Malik (marfu'): The cure for 'irq al-nasa (sciatica) is the tail of an Arab sheep, which is melted, then divided into three parts, then one part is drunk every day on an empty stomach."
"2313","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (marfu'): Evil omen is in the house, the woman, and the horse."
"2314","[AI-translation] Khudri who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: My brother's stomach has become loose. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Give him honey to drink. He gave him to drink, then he came to him and said: I gave him honey to drink, but it only increased his looseness. He said this to him three times, then he came a fourth time and he said: Give him honey to drink. He said: I have indeed given him to drink, and it only increased his looseness. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah has spoken the truth, and your brother's stomach has lied. So he gave him to drink, and he recovered."
"2315","[AI-translation] Narrated from Aisha (marfu'): The plague is martyrdom for my Ummah, and a stab for your enemies among the jinn; it is a swelling like the swelling of camels, emerging in the armpits and the groin. Whoever dies in it dies a martyr, and whoever remains in it is like the one stationed in the path of Allah, and whoever flees from it is like the one fleeing from the battlefield."
"2316","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Awf (marfu'): The one who visits the sick is in the harvest of Paradise, and when he sits with him, mercy envelops him."
"2317","[AI-translation] Narrated from Aisha: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, entered upon her while a woman was treating her or performing ruqyah upon her, so he said: Treat her with the Book of Allah."
"2318","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: Upon you is ithmid (antimony) before sleep, for it clears the vision and grows the hair."
"2319","[AI-translation] From 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, marfu'an: Adhere to antimony (ithmid), for it makes the hair grow, removes specks, and purifies the sight."
"2320","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, marfu'an: Adhere to the milk of cows, for they graze from every tree, and it is a healing from every disease."
"2321","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu'an: Adhere to this black seed, for in it is a healing from every disease except death."
"2322","[AI-translation] From Abu Buraydah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Adhere to the black seed, which is the shuniz, for in it is a healing."
"2323","[AI-translation] From Abu Ubayy ibn Umm Haram who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) saying: Adhere to the sana and the sanut, for in them is a healing from every disease except death. It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is as-Sam?"" He said, ""Death."
"2324","[AI-translation] Khudri, marfu'an: Visit the sick and follow the funeral processions, for they remind you of the Hereafter."
"2325","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: The evil eye puts a man in the grave and a camel in the pot. Narrated from the hadith of Jabir and Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"2326","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu'an: The evil eye is true."
"2327","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu'an: The evil eye is true; it brings down the bald one (al-haliq)."
"2328","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu'an: The evil eye is true, and if anything were to precede destiny, the evil eye would precede it. And if you are asked to wash, then wash."
"2329","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah that he heard the Messenger of Allah regarding the black seed: A cure for every disease except death."
"2330","[AI-translation] From Aishah from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: In the 'ajwah of al-'Aliyah taken first thing in the morning on an empty stomach, there is a cure for every magic or poison."
"2331","[AI-translation] 'Adawiyyah who said: I entered upon Aishah and asked her about fleeing from the plague. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Fleeing from the plague is like fleeing from battle."
"2332","[AI-translation] From Anas: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to be cupped on the al-akhda'ayn and al-kahil, and he used to be cupped on the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first."
"2333","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to be cupped on his head, and he named it Umm Mughith."
"2334","[AI-translation] From Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to command her to seek ruqyah for the evil eye."
"2335","[AI-translation] From Aishah who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to command the one who cast the evil eye to perform ablution, then the one affected by the evil eye would wash with it."
"2336","Aisha said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was seized by pain in his side, and it became very severe. One day it seized him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) fainted, until we thought he had died on the bed. So we forced medicine into his mouth. When he recovered, he realized we had forced medicine on him. He said: ""Did you think that Allah would afflict me with pleurisy? Allah would not give it authority over me. By Allah, no one will remain in the house except you will force medicine on him, except my uncle Al-Abbas."" She said: So no one remained in the house except they were forced to take medicine. Then a woman from among his wives said: ""I am fasting!"" They said: ""Do you think we will leave you? When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'No one will remain in the house except he will be forced to take medicine.'"" So we forced her to take medicine while she was fasting."
"2337","[AI-translation] From Ali who said: A scorpion stung the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was praying. When he finished, he said: ""May Allah curse the scorpion. It does not spare a praying person or anyone else."" Then he called for water and salt, and began to wipe it over the sting, reciting: Say, O you disbelievers (1), Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak (1), Say, He is Allah, the One (1)."
"2338","[AI-translation] From Ubaydullah bin Amr, raising it: Were it not for what touched it of the impurities of the pre-Islamic period, no one with an affliction would have touched it except that he would be cured. And there is nothing on earth from Paradise except it."
"2339","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Masud, reaching the Prophet (peace be upon him): Allah has not sent down a disease except that He has sent down for it a cure; whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it."
"2340","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) entered and heard the voice of a baby crying, so he said: ""What is the matter with your baby that he is crying? Why did you not seek ruqyah for him against the evil eye?"
"2341","[AI-translation] From Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah, that they both heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""No weariness, nor fatigue, nor sickness, nor grief, even the worry that worries him, afflicts a believer except that his sins are expiated by it."
"2342","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu'an: ""Whoever is cupped on the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first, it is a cure for every disease."
"2343","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever treats himself with something unlawful, Allah has not made a cure in it for him."
"2344","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Whoever practices medicine and no knowledge of medicine is known from him, then he is liable."
"2345","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever visits a sick person remains wading in mercy until he sits; and when he sits, he is immersed in it."
"2346","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu'an: ""Do not prolong looking at those afflicted with leprosy."
"2347","[AI-translation] Sa'ib or Umm al-Musayyib, and said: ""What is wrong with you, O Umm al-Sa'ib or O Umm al-Musayyib, that you are shivering?"" She said: ""It is the fever; may Allah not bless it."" He said: ""Do not curse the fever, for it removes the sins of the children of Adam just as the bellows removes the impurities of iron."
"2348","[AI-translation] From Mikhmar ibn Mu'awiyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""There is no evil omen, and good omen may be in three things: the woman, the horse, and the house."
"2349","[AI-translation] Taymi, my father narrated to me, marfu'an: ""There is nothing in the owl, and the evil eye is true, and the truest of omens is the good omen."
"2350","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu': ""The sick should not be brought to the healthy."
"2351","[AI-translation] As, he said: I complained to the Messenger of Allah about forgetting the Quran, so he struck my chest with his hand and said: ""O Satan! Get out of the chest of Uthman."" (He did that three times.) Uthman said: I did not forget anything of it afterwards when I wished to remember it."
"2352","[AI-translation] Mundir bint Qais Al-Ansariyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah entered upon me while with him was Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and Ali was convalescent. We had some hanging clusters of dates. The Messenger of Allah stood up to eat from them, and Ali stood up to eat. The Messenger of Allah kept saying to Ali: ""Stop, for you are recovering,"" until Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, stopped. She said: And I prepared some barley and chard and brought it. The Messenger of Allah said: ""O Ali! Partake of this, for it is more beneficial for you."
